-- NRSV-CE OLD TESTAMENT BIBLE VERSES (PART 5)

She left him there for the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

"My heart exults in the LORD;  
    my strength is exalted in my God.  
My mouth derides my enemies,  
    because I rejoice in my victory.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Hannah"s Prayer'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 2, '"There is no Holy One like the LORD,  
    no one besides you;  
    there is no Rock like our God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 3, 'Talk no more so very proudly,  
    let not arrogance come from your mouth;  
for the LORD is a God of knowledge,  
    and by him actions are weighed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 4, 'The bows of the mighty are broken,  
    but the feeble gird on strength.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 5, 'Those who were full have hired themselves out for bread,  
    but those who were hungry are fat with spoil.  
The barren has borne seven,  
    but she who has many children is forlorn.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 6, 'The LORD kills and brings to life;  
    he brings down to Sheol and raises up.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 7, 'The LORD makes poor and makes rich;  
    he brings low, he also exalts.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 8, 'He raises up the poor from the dust;  
    he lifts the needy from the ash heap,  
to make them sit with princes  
    and inherit a seat of honor.  
For the pillars of the earth are the LORD"s,  
    and on them he has set the world.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 9, '"He will guard the feet of his faithful ones,  
    but the wicked shall be cut off in darkness;  
    for not by might does one prevail.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 10, 'The LORD! His adversaries shall be shattered;  
    the Most High will thunder in heaven.  
The LORD will judge the ends of the earth;  
    he will give strength to his king,  
    and exalt the power of his anointed."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 11, 'Then Elkanah went home to Ramah, while the boy remained to minister to the LORD, in the presence of the priest Eli.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Eli"s Wicked Sons'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 12, 'Now the sons of Eli were scoundrels; they had no regard for the LORD', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 13, 'or for the duties of the priests to the people. When anyone offered sacrifice, the priest"s servant would come, while the meat was boiling, with a three-pronged fork in his hand,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 14, 'and he would thrust it into the pan, or kettle, or caldron, or pot; all that the fork brought up the priest would take for himself. This is what they did at Shiloh to all the Israelites who came there.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 15, 'Moreover, before the fat was burned, the priest"s servant would come and say to the one who was sacrificing, "Give meat for the priest to roast; for he will not accept boiled meat from you, but only raw."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 16, 'And if the man said to him, "Let them burn the fat first, and then take whatever you wish," he would say, "No, you must give it now; if not, I will take it by force."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 17, 'Thus the sin of the young men was very great in the sight of the LORD; for they treated the offerings of the LORD with contempt.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 18, 'Samuel was ministering before the LORD, a boy wearing a linen ephod.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Child Samuel at Shiloh'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 19, 'His mother used to make for him a little robe and take it to him each year, when she went up with her husband to offer the yearly sacrifice.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 20, 'Then Eli would bless Elkanah and his wife, and say, "May the LORD repay you with children by this woman for the gift that she made to the LORD"; and then they would return to their home.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 21, 'And the LORD took note of Hannah; she conceived and bore three sons and two daughters. And the boy Samuel grew up in the presence of the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 22, 'Now Eli was very old. He heard all that his sons were doing to all Israel, and how they lay with the women who served at the entrance to the tent of meeting.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Prophecy against Eli"s Household'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 23, 'He said to them, "Why do you do such things? For I hear of your evil dealings from all these people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 24, 'No, my sons; it is not a good report that I hear the people of the LORD spreading abroad.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 25, 'If one person sins against another, someone can intercede for the sinner with the LORD; but if someone sins against the LORD, who can make intercession?" But they would not listen to the voice of their father; for it was the will of the LORD to kill them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 26, 'Now the boy Samuel continued to grow both in stature and in favor with the LORD and with the people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 27, 'A man of God came to Eli and said to him, "Thus the LORD has said, "I revealed myself to the family of your ancestor in Egypt when they were slaves to the house of Pharaoh.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 28, 'I chose him out of all the tribes of Israel to be my priest, to go up to my altar, to offer incense, to wear an ephod before me; and I gave to the family of your ancestor all my offerings by fire from the people of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 29, 'Why then look with greedy eye at my sacrifices and my offerings that I commanded, and honor your sons more than me by fattening yourselves on the choicest parts of every offering of my people Israel?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 30, 'Therefore the LORD the God of Israel declares: "I promised that your family and the family of your ancestor should go in and out before me forever"; but now the LORD declares: "Far be it from me; for those who honor me I will honor, and those who despise me shall be treated with contempt.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 31, 'See, a time is coming when I will cut off your strength and the strength of your ancestor"s family, so that no one in your family will live to old age.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 32, 'Then in distress you will look with greedy eye on all the prosperity that shall be bestowed upon Israel; and no one in your family shall ever live to old age.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 33, 'The only one of you whom I shall not cut off from my altar shall be spared to weep out his eyes and grieve his heart; all the members of your household shall die by the sword.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 34, 'The fate of your two sons, Hophni and Phinehas, shall be the sign to you--both of them shall die on the same day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 35, 'I will raise up for myself a faithful priest, who shall do according to what is in my heart and in my mind. I will build him a sure house, and he shall go in and out before my anointed one forever.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 2, 36, 'Everyone who is left in your family shall come to implore him for a piece of silver or a loaf of bread, and shall say, Please put me in one of the priest"s places, that I may eat a morsel of bread.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


In those days the Philistines mustered for war against Israel, and Israel went out to battle against them; they encamped at Ebenezer, and the Philistines encamped at Aphek.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Ark of God Captured'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 2, 'The Philistines drew up in line against Israel, and when the battle was joined, Israel was defeated by the Philistines, who killed about four thousand men on the field of battle.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 3, 'When the troops came to the camp, the elders of Israel said, "Why has the LORD put us to rout today before the Philistines? Let us bring the ark of the covenant of the LORD here from Shiloh, so that he may come among us and save us from the power of our enemies."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 4, 'So the people sent to Shiloh, and brought from there the ark of the covenant of the LORD of hosts, who is enthroned on the cherubim. The two sons of Eli, Hophni and Phinehas, were there with the ark of the covenant of God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 5, 'When the ark of the covenant of the LORD came into the camp, all Israel gave a mighty shout, so that the earth resounded.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 6, 'When the Philistines heard the noise of the shouting, they said, "What does this great shouting in the camp of the Hebrews mean?" When they learned that the ark of the LORD had come to the camp,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 7, 'the Philistines were afraid; for they said, "Gods have come into the camp." They also said, "Woe to us! For nothing like this has happened before.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 8, 'Woe to us! Who can deliver us from the power of these mighty gods? These are the gods who struck the Egyptians with every sort of plague in the wilderness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 9, 'Take courage, and be men, O Philistines, in order not to become slaves to the Hebrews as they have been to you; be men and fight."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 10, 'So the Philistines fought; Israel was defeated, and they fled, everyone to his home. There was a very great slaughter, for there fell of Israel thirty thousand foot soldiers.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 11, 'The ark of God was captured; and the two sons of Eli, Hophni and Phinehas, died.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 12, 'A man of Benjamin ran from the battle line, and came to Shiloh the same day, with his clothes torn and with earth upon his head.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Death of Eli'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 13, 'When he arrived, Eli was sitting upon his seat by the road watching, for his heart trembled for the ark of God. When the man came into the city and told the news, all the city cried out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 14, 'When Eli heard the sound of the outcry, he said, "What is this uproar?" Then the man came quickly and told Eli.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 15, 'Now Eli was ninety-eight years old and his eyes were set, so that he could not see.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 16, 'The man said to Eli, "I have just come from the battle; I fled from the battle today." He said, "How did it go, my son?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 17, 'The messenger replied, "Israel has fled before the Philistines, and there has also been a great slaughter among the troops; your two sons also, Hophni and Phinehas, are dead, and the ark of God has been captured."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 18, 'When he mentioned the ark of God, Eli fell over backward from his seat by the side of the gate; and his neck was broken and he died, for he was an old man, and heavy. He had judged Israel forty years.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 19, 'Now his daughter-in-law, the wife of Phinehas, was pregnant, about to give birth. When she heard the news that the ark of God was captured, and that her father-in-law and her husband were dead, she bowed and gave birth; for her labor pains overwhelmed her.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 20, 'As she was about to die, the women attending her said to her, "Do not be afraid, for you have borne a son." But she did not answer or give heed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 21, 'She named the child Ichabod, meaning, "The glory has departed from Israel," because the ark of God had been captured and because of her father-in-law and her husband.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 4, 22, 'She said, "The glory has departed from Israel, for the ark of God has been captured."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);





So Saul ate with Samuel that day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 9, 25, 'When they came down from the shrine into the town, a bed was spread for Saul on the roof, and he lay down to sleep.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 9, 26, 'Then at the break of dawn Samuel called to Saul upon the roof, "Get up, so that I may send you on your way." Saul got up, and both he and Samuel went out into the street.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 9, 27, 'As they were going down to the outskirts of the town, Samuel said to Saul, "Tell the boy to go on before us, and when he has passed on, stop here yourself for a while, that I may make known to you the word of God."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Samuel Anoints Saul');

Now Nahash, king of the Ammonites, had been grievously oppressing the Gadites and the Reubenites. He would gouge out the right eye of each of them and would not grant Israel a deliverer. No one was left of the Israelites across the Jordan whose right eye Nahash, king of the Ammonites, had not gouged out. But there were seven thousand men who had escaped from the Ammonites and had entered Jabesh-gilead.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);



Saul counted the people who were present with him, about six hundred men.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Preparations for Battle'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 13, 16, 'Saul, his son Jonathan, and the people who were present with them stayed in Geba of Benjamin; but the Philistines encamped at Michmash.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 13, 17, 'And raiders came out of the camp of the Philistines in three companies; one company turned toward Ophrah, to the land of Shual,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 13, 18, 'another company turned toward Beth-horon, and another company turned toward the mountain that looks down upon the valley of Zeboim toward the wilderness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 13, 19, 'Now there was no smith to be found throughout all the land of Israel; for the Philistines said, "The Hebrews must not make swords or spears for themselves";', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 13, 20, 'so all the Israelites went down to the Philistines to sharpen their plowshares, mattocks, axes, or sickles;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 13, 21, 'The charge was two-thirds of a shekel for the plowshares and for the mattocks, and one-third of a shekel for sharpening the axes and for setting the goads.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 13, 22, 'So on the day of the battle neither sword nor spear was to be found in the possession of any of the people with Saul and Jonathan; but Saul and his son Jonathan had them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 13, 23, 'Now a garrison of the Philistines had gone out to the pass of Michmash.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Jonathan Surprises and Routs the Philistines');

The battle passed beyond Beth-aven, and the troops with Saul numbered altogether about ten thousand men. The battle spread out over the hill country of Ephraim.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 24, 'Now Saul committed a very rash act on that day. He had laid an oath on the troops, saying, "Cursed be anyone who eats food before it is evening and I have been avenged on my enemies." So none of the troops tasted food.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Saul"s Rash Oath'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 25, 'All the troops came upon a honeycomb; and there was honey on the ground.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 26, 'When the troops came upon the honeycomb, the honey was dripping out; but they did not put their hands to their mouths, for they feared the oath.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 27, 'But Jonathan had not heard his father charge the troops with the oath; so he extended the staff that was in his hand, and dipped the tip of it in the honeycomb, and put his hand to his mouth; and his eyes brightened.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 28, 'Then one of the soldiers said, "Your father strictly charged the troops with an oath, saying, "Cursed be anyone who eats food this day." And so the troops are faint."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 29, 'Then Jonathan said, "My father has troubled the land; see how my eyes have brightened because I tasted a little of this honey.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 30, 'How much better if today the troops had eaten freely of the spoil taken from their enemies; for now the slaughter among the Philistines has not been great."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 31, 'After they had struck down the Philistines that day from Michmash to Aijalon, the troops were very faint;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 32, 'so the troops flew upon the spoil, and took sheep and oxen and calves, and slaughtered them on the ground; and the troops ate them with the blood.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 33, 'Then it was reported to Saul, "Look, the troops are sinning against the LORD by eating with the blood." And he said, "You have dealt treacherously; roll a large stone before me here."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 34, 'Saul said, "Disperse yourselves among the troops, and say to them, "Let all bring their oxen or their sheep, and slaughter them here, and eat; and do not sin against the LORD by eating with the blood."" So all of the troops brought their oxen with them that night, and slaughtered them there.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 35, 'And Saul built an altar to the LORD; it was the first altar that he built to the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 36, 'Then Saul said, "Let us go down after the Philistines by night and despoil them until the morning light; let us not leave one of them." They said, "Do whatever seems good to you." But the priest said, "Let us draw near to God here."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Jonathan in Danger of Death'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 37, 'So Saul inquired of God, "Shall I go down after the Philistines? Will you give them into the hand of Israel?" But he did not answer him that day.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 38, 'Saul said, "Come here, all you leaders of the people; and let us find out how this sin has arisen today.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 39, 'For as the LORD lives who saves Israel, even if it is in my son Jonathan, he shall surely die!" But there was no one among all the people who answered him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 40, 'He said to all Israel, "You shall be on one side, and I and my son Jonathan will be on the other side." The people said to Saul, "Do what seems good to you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 41, 'Then Saul said, "O LORD God of Israel, why have you not answered your servant today? If this guilt is in me or in my son Jonathan, O LORD God of Israel, give Urim; but if this guilt is in your people Israel, give Thummim." And Jonathan and Saul were indicated by the lot, but the people were cleared.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 42, 'Then Saul said, "Cast the lot between me and my son Jonathan." And Jonathan was taken.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 43, 'Then Saul said to Jonathan, "Tell me what you have done." Jonathan told him, "I tasted a little honey with the tip of the staff that was in my hand; here I am, I will die."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 44, 'Saul said, "God do so to me and more also; you shall surely die, Jonathan!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 45, 'Then the people said to Saul, "Shall Jonathan die, who has accomplished this great victory in Israel? Far from it! As the LORD lives, not one hair of his head shall fall to the ground; for he has worked with God today." So the people ransomed Jonathan, and he did not die.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 46, 'Then Saul withdrew from pursuing the Philistines; and the Philistines went to their own place.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 47, 'When Saul had taken the kingship over Israel, he fought against all his enemies on every side--against Moab, against the Ammonites, against Edom, against the kings of Zobah, and against the Philistines; wherever he turned he routed them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Saul"s Continuing Wars'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 48, 'He did valiantly, and struck down the Amalekites, and rescued Israel out of the hands of those who plundered them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 49, 'Now the sons of Saul were Jonathan, Ishvi, and Malchishua; and the names of his two daughters were these: the name of the firstborn was Merab, and the name of the younger, Michal.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 50, 'The name of Saul"s wife was Ahinoam daughter of Ahimaaz. And the name of the commander of his army was Abner son of Ner, Saul"s uncle;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 51, 'Kish was the father of Saul, and Ner the father of Abner was the son of Abiel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 14, 52, 'There was hard fighting against the Philistines all the days of Saul; and when Saul saw any strong or valiant warrior, he took him into his service.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

"Has the LORD as great delight in burnt offerings and sacrifices,  
    as in obedience to the voice of the LORD?  
Surely, to obey is better than sacrifice,  
    and to heed than the fat of rams.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 23, 'For rebellion is no less a sin than divination,  
    and stubbornness is like iniquity and idolatry.  
Because you have rejected the word of the LORD,  
    he has also rejected you from being king."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 24, 'Saul said to Samuel, "I have sinned; for I have transgressed the commandment of the LORD and your words, because I feared the people and obeyed their voice.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 25, 'Now therefore, I pray, pardon my sin, and return with me, so that I may worship the LORD."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 26, 'Samuel said to Saul, "I will not return with you; for you have rejected the word of the LORD, and the LORD has rejected you from being king over Israel."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 27, 'As Samuel turned to go away, Saul caught hold of the hem of his robe, and it tore.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 28, 'And Samuel said to him, "The LORD has torn the kingdom of Israel from you this very day, and has given it to a neighbor of yours, who is better than you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 29, 'Moreover the Glory of Israel will not recant or change his mind; for he is not a mortal, that he should change his mind."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 30, 'Then Saul said, "I have sinned; yet honor me now before the elders of my people and before Israel, and return with me, so that I may worship the LORD your God."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 31, 'So Samuel turned back after Saul; and Saul worshiped the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 32, 'Then Samuel said, "Bring Agag king of the Amalekites here to me." And Agag came to him haltingly. Agag said, "Surely this is the bitterness of death."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 33, 'But Samuel said,
"As your sword has made women childless,  
    so your mother shall be childless among women."
And Samuel hewed Agag in pieces before the LORD in Gilgal.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 34, 'Then Samuel went to Ramah; and Saul went up to his house in Gibeah of Saul.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 15, 35, 'Samuel did not see Saul again until the day of his death, but Samuel grieved over Saul. And the LORD was sorry that he had made Saul king over Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


When the Philistines saw that their champion was dead, they fled.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 17, 52, 'The troops of Israel and Judah rose up with a shout and pursued the Philistines as far as Gath and the gates of Ekron, so that the wounded Philistines fell on the way from Shaaraim as far as Gath and Ekron.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 17, 53, 'The Israelites came back from chasing the Philistines, and they plundered their camp.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 17, 54, 'David took the head of the Philistine and brought it to Jerusalem; but he put his armor in his tent.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 17, 55, 'When Saul saw David go out against the Philistine, he said to Abner, the commander of the army, "Abner, whose son is this young man?" Abner said, "As your soul lives, O king, I do not know."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 17, 56, 'The king said, "Inquire whose son the stripling is."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 17, 57, 'On David"s return from killing the Philistine, Abner took him and brought him before Saul, with the head of the Philistine in his hand.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 17, 58, 'Saul said to him, "Whose son are you, young man?" And David answered, "I am the son of your servant Jesse the Bethlehemite."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

"Saul has killed his thousands,  
    and David his ten thousands."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 8, 'Saul was very angry, for this saying displeased him. He said, "They have ascribed to David ten thousands, and to me they have ascribed thousands; what more can he have but the kingdom?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 9, 'So Saul eyed David from that day on.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 10, 'The next day an evil spirit from God rushed upon Saul, and he raved within his house, while David was playing the lyre, as he did day by day. Saul had his spear in his hand;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Saul Tries to Kill David'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 11, 'and Saul threw the spear, for he thought, "I will pin David to the wall." But David eluded him twice.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 12, 'Saul was afraid of David, because the LORD was with him but had departed from Saul.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 13, 'So Saul removed him from his presence, and made him a commander of a thousand; and David marched out and came in, leading the army.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 14, 'David had success in all his undertakings; for the LORD was with him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 15, 'When Saul saw that he had great success, he stood in awe of him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 16, 'But all Israel and Judah loved David; for it was he who marched out and came in leading them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 17, 'Then Saul said to David, "Here is my elder daughter Merab; I will give her to you as a wife; only be valiant for me and fight the LORD"s battles." For Saul thought, "I will not raise a hand against him; let the Philistines deal with him."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'David Marries Michal'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 18, 'David said to Saul, "Who am I and who are my kinsfolk, my father"s family in Israel, that I should be son-in-law to the king?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 19, 'But at the time when Saul"s daughter Merab should have been given to David, she was given to Adriel the Meholathite as a wife.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 20, 'Now Saul"s daughter Michal loved David. Saul was told, and the thing pleased him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 21, 'Saul thought, "Let me give her to him that she may be a snare for him and that the hand of the Philistines may be against him." Therefore Saul said to David a second time, "You shall now be my son-in-law."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 22, 'Saul commanded his servants, "Speak to David in private and say, "See, the king is delighted with you, and all his servants love you; now then, become the king"s son-in-law.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 23, 'So Saul"s servants reported these words to David in private. And David said, "Does it seem to you a little thing to become the king"s son-in-law, seeing that I am a poor man and of no repute?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 24, 'The servants of Saul told him, "This is what David said."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 25, 'Then Saul said, "Thus shall you say to David, "The king desires no marriage present except a hundred foreskins of the Philistines, that he may be avenged on the king"s enemies."" Now Saul planned to make David fall by the hand of the Philistines.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 26, 'When his servants told David these words, David was well pleased to be the king"s son-in-law. Before the time had expired,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 27, 'David rose and went, along with his men, and killed one hundred of the Philistines; and David brought their foreskins, which were given in full number to the king, that he might become the king"s son-in-law. Saul gave him his daughter Michal as a wife.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 28, 'But when Saul realized that the LORD was with David, and that Saul"s daughter Michal loved him,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 29, 'Saul was still more afraid of David. So Saul was David"s enemy from that time forward.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 18, 30, 'Then the commanders of the Philistines came out to battle; and as often as they came out, David had more success than all the servants of Saul, so that his fame became very great.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);



"Saul has killed his thousands,  
    and David his ten thousands"?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 21, 12, 'David took these words to heart and was very much afraid of King Achish of Gath.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 21, 13, 'So he changed his behavior before them; he pretended to be mad when in their presence. He scratched marks on the doors of the gate, and let his spittle run down his beard.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 21, 14, 'Achish said to his servants, "Look, you see the man is mad; why then have you brought him to me?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 21, 15, 'Do I lack madmen, that you have brought this fellow to play the madman in my presence? Shall this fellow come into my house?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


David and his men were in the wilderness of Maon, in the Arabah to the south of Jeshimon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 23, 25, 'Saul and his men went to search for him. When David was told, he went down to the rock and stayed in the wilderness of Maon. When Saul heard that, he pursued David into the wilderness of Maon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 23, 26, 'Saul went on one side of the mountain, and David and his men on the other side of the mountain. David was hurrying to get away from Saul, while Saul and his men were closing in on David and his men to capture them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 23, 27, 'Then a messenger came to Saul, saying, "Hurry and come; for the Philistines have made a raid on the land."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 23, 28, 'So Saul stopped pursuing David, and went against the Philistines; therefore that place was called the Rock of Escape.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 23, 29, 'David then went up from there, and lived in the strongholds of En-gedi.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


Then David got up and went down to the wilderness of Paran.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Death of Samuel'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 2, 'There was a man in Maon, whose property was in Carmel. The man was very rich; he had three thousand sheep and a thousand goats. He was shearing his sheep in Carmel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'David and the Wife of Nabal'),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 3, 'Now the name of the man was Nabal, and the name of his wife Abigail. The woman was clever and beautiful, but the man was surly and mean; he was a Calebite.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 4, 'David heard in the wilderness that Nabal was shearing his sheep.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 5, 'So David sent ten young men; and David said to the young men, "Go up to Carmel, and go to Nabal, and greet him in my name.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 6, 'Thus you shall salute him: "Peace be to you, and peace be to your house, and peace be to all that you have.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 7, 'I hear that you have shearers; now your shepherds have been with us, and we did them no harm, and they missed nothing, all the time they were in Carmel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 8, 'Ask your young men, and they will tell you. Therefore let my young men find favor in your sight; for we have come on a feast day. Please give whatever you have at hand to your servants and to your son David.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 9, 'When David"s young men came, they said all this to Nabal in the name of David; and then they waited.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 10, 'But Nabal answered David"s servants, "Who is David? Who is the son of Jesse? There are many servants today who are breaking away from their masters.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 11, 'Shall I take my bread and my water and the meat that I have butchered for my shearers, and give it to men who come from I do not know where?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 12, 'So David"s young men turned away, and came back and told him all this.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 13, 'David said to his men, "Every man strap on his sword!" And every one of them strapped on his sword; David also strapped on his sword; and about four hundred men went up after David, while two hundred remained with the baggage.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 14, 'But one of the young men told Abigail, Nabal"s wife, "David sent messengers out of the wilderness to salute our master; and he shouted insults at them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 15, 'Yet the men were very good to us, and we suffered no harm, and we never missed anything when we were in the fields, as long as we were with them;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 16, 'they were a wall to us both by night and by day, all the while we were with them keeping the sheep.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 17, 'Now therefore know this and consider what you should do; for evil has been decided against our master and against all his house; he is so ill-natured that no one can speak to him."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 18, 'Then Abigail hurried and took two hundred loaves, two skins of wine, five sheep ready dressed, five measures of parched grain, one hundred clusters of raisins, and two hundred cakes of figs. She loaded them on donkeys', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 19, 'and said to her young men, "Go on ahead of me; I am coming after you." But she did not tell her husband Nabal.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 20, 'As she rode on the donkey and came down under cover of the mountain, David and his men came down toward her; and she met them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 21, 'Now David had said, "Surely it was in vain that I protected all that this fellow has in the wilderness, so that nothing was missed of all that belonged to him; but he has returned me evil for good.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 22, 'God do so to David and more also, if by morning I leave so much as one male of all who belong to him."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 23, 'When Abigail saw David, she hurried and alighted from the donkey, and fell before David on her face, bowing to the ground.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 24, 'She fell at his feet and said, "Upon me alone, my lord, be the guilt; please let your servant speak in your ears, and hear the words of your servant.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 25, 'My lord, do not take seriously this ill-natured fellow, Nabal; for as his name is, so is he; Nabal is his name, and folly is with him; but I, your servant, did not see the young men of my lord, whom you sent.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 26, '"Now then, my lord, as the LORD lives, and as you yourself live, since the LORD has restrained you from bloodguilt and from taking vengeance with your own hand, now let your enemies and those who seek to do evil to my lord be like Nabal.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 27, 'And now let this present that your servant has brought to my lord be given to the young men who follow my lord.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 28, 'Please forgive the trespass of your servant; for the LORD will certainly make my lord a sure house, because my lord is fighting the battles of the LORD; and evil shall not be found in you so long as you live.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 29, 'If anyone should rise up to pursue you and to seek your life, the life of my lord shall be bound in the bundle of the living under the care of the LORD your God; but the lives of your enemies he shall sling out as from the hollow of a sling.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 30, 'When the LORD has done to my lord according to all the good that he has spoken concerning you, and has appointed you prince over Israel,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 31, 'my lord shall have no cause of grief, or pangs of conscience, for having shed blood without cause or for having saved himself. And when the LORD has dealt well with my lord, then remember your servant."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 32, 'David said to Abigail, "Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, who sent you to meet me today!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 33, 'Blessed be your good sense, and blessed be you, who have kept me today from bloodguilt and from avenging myself by my own hand!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 34, 'For as surely as the LORD the God of Israel lives, who has restrained me from hurting you, unless you had hurried and come to meet me, truly by morning there would not have been left to Nabal so much as one male."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 35, 'Then David received from her hand what she had brought him; he said to her, "Go up to your house in peace; see, I have heeded your voice, and I have granted your petition."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 36, 'Abigail came to Nabal; he was holding a feast in his house, like the feast of a king. Nabal"s heart was merry within him, for he was very drunk; so she told him nothing at all until the morning light.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 37, 'In the morning, when the wine had gone out of Nabal, his wife told him these things, and his heart died within him; he became like a stone.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 38, 'About ten days later the LORD struck Nabal, and he died.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 39, 'When David heard that Nabal was dead, he said, "Blessed be the LORD who has judged the case of Nabal"s insult to me, and has kept back his servant from evil; the LORD has returned the evildoing of Nabal upon his own head." Then David sent and wooed Abigail, to make her his wife.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 40, 'When David"s servants came to Abigail at Carmel, they said to her, "David has sent us to you to take you to him as his wife."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 41, 'She rose and bowed down, with her face to the ground, and said, "Your servant is a slave to wash the feet of the servants of my lord."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 42, 'Abigail got up hurriedly and rode away on a donkey; her five maids attended her. She went after the messengers of David and became his wife.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 43, 'David also married Ahinoam of Jezreel; both of them became his wives.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 25, 44, 'Saul had given his daughter Michal, David"s wife, to Palti son of Laish, who was from Gallim.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);




"Saul has killed his thousands,  
    and David his ten thousands"?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 29, 6, 'Then Achish called David and said to him, "As the LORD lives, you have been honest, and to me it seems right that you should march out and in with me in the campaign; for I have found nothing wrong in you from the day of your coming to me until today. Nevertheless the lords do not approve of you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 29, 7, 'So go back now; and go peaceably; do nothing to displease the lords of the Philistines."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 29, 8, 'David said to Achish, "But what have I done? What have you found in your servant from the day I entered your service until now, that I should not go and fight against the enemies of my lord the king?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 29, 9, 'Achish replied to David, "I know that you are as blameless in my sight as an angel of God; nevertheless, the commanders of the Philistines have said, "He shall not go up with us to the battle."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 29, 10, 'Now then rise early in the morning, you and the servants of your lord who came with you, and go to the place that I appointed for you. As for the evil report, do not take it to heart, for you have done well before me. Start early in the morning, and leave as soon as you have light."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(9, '1 Sam', '1 Samuel', 29, 11, 'So David set out with his men early in the morning, to return to the land of the Philistines. But the Philistines went up to Jezreel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);



    How the mighty have fallen!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 1, 20, 'Tell it not in Gath,  
    proclaim it not in the streets of Ashkelon;  
or the daughters of the Philistines will rejoice,  
    the daughters of the uncircumcised will exult.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 1, 21, 'You mountains of Gilboa,  
    let there be no dew or rain upon you,  
    nor bounteous fields!  
For there the shield of the mighty was defiled,  
    the shield of Saul, anointed with oil no more.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 1, 22, 'From the blood of the slain,  
    from the fat of the mighty,  
the bow of Jonathan did not turn back,  
    nor the sword of Saul return empty.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 1, 23, 'Saul and Jonathan, beloved and lovely!  
    In life and in death they were not divided;  
they were swifter than eagles,  
    they were stronger than lions.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 1, 24, 'O daughters of Israel, weep over Saul,  
    who clothed you with crimson, in luxury,  
    who put ornaments of gold on your apparel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 1, 25, 'How the mighty have fallen  
    in the midst of the battle!
Jonathan lies slain upon your high places.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 1, 26, 'I am distressed for you, my brother Jonathan;  
greatly beloved were you to me;  
    your love to me was wonderful,  
    passing the love of women.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 1, 27, 'How the mighty have fallen,  
    and the weapons of war perished!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

When they told David, "It was the people of Jabesh-gilead who buried Saul,"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 5, 'David sent messengers to the people of Jabesh-gilead, and said to them, "May you be blessed by the LORD, because you showed this loyalty to Saul your lord, and buried him!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 6, 'Now may the LORD show steadfast love and faithfulness to you! And I too will reward you because you have done this thing.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 7, 'Therefore let your hands be strong, and be valiant; for Saul your lord is dead, and the house of Judah has anointed me king over them."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 8, 'But Abner son of Ner, commander of Saul"s army, had taken Ishbaal son of Saul, and brought him over to Mahanaim.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Ishbaal King of Israel'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 9, 'He made him king over Gilead, the Ashurites, Jezreel, Ephraim, Benjamin, and over all Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 10, 'Ishbaal, Saul"s son, was forty years old when he began to reign over Israel, and he reigned two years. But the house of Judah followed David.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 11, 'The time that David was king in Hebron over the house of Judah was seven years and six months.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 12, 'Abner son of Ner, and the servants of Ishbaal son of Saul, went out from Mahanaim to Gibeon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Battle of Gibeon'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 13, 'Joab son of Zeruiah, and the servants of David, went out and met them at the pool of Gibeon. One group sat on one side of the pool, while the other sat on the other side of the pool.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 14, 'Abner said to Joab, "Let the young men come forward and have a contest before us." Joab said, "Let them come forward."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 15, 'So they came forward and were counted as they passed by, twelve for Benjamin and Ishbaal son of Saul, and twelve of the servants of David.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 16, 'Each grasped his opponent by the head, and thrust his sword in his opponent"s side; so they fell down together. Therefore that place was called Helkath-hazzurim, which is at Gibeon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 17, 'The battle was very fierce that day; and Abner and the men of Israel were beaten by the servants of David.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 18, 'The three sons of Zeruiah were there, Joab, Abishai, and Asahel. Now Asahel was as swift of foot as a wild gazelle.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 19, 'Asahel pursued Abner, turning neither to the right nor to the left as he followed him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 20, 'Then Abner looked back and said, "Is it you, Asahel?" He answered, "Yes, it is."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 21, 'Abner said to him, "Turn to your right or to your left, and seize one of the young men, and take his spoil." But Asahel would not turn away from following him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 22, 'Abner said again to Asahel, "Turn away from following me; why should I strike you to the ground? How then could I show my face to your brother Joab?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 23, 'But he refused to turn away. So Abner struck him in the stomach with the butt of his spear, so that the spear came out at his back. He fell there, and died where he lay. And all those who came to the place where Asahel had fallen and died, stood still.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 24, 'But Joab and Abishai pursued Abner. As the sun was going down they came to the hill of Ammah, which lies before Giah on the way to the wilderness of Gibeon.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 25, 'The Benjaminites rallied around Abner and formed a single band; they took their stand on the top of a hill.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 26, 'Then Abner called to Joab, "Is the sword to keep devouring forever? Do you not know that the end will be bitter? How long will it be before you order your people to turn from the pursuit of their kinsmen?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 27, 'Joab said, "As God lives, if you had not spoken, the people would have continued to pursue their kinsmen, not stopping until morning."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 28, 'Joab sounded the trumpet and all the people stopped; they no longer pursued Israel or engaged in battle any further.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 29, 'Abner and his men traveled all that night through the Arabah; they crossed the Jordan, and, marching the whole forenoon, they came to Mahanaim.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 30, 'Joab returned from the pursuit of Abner; and when he had gathered all the people together, there were missing of David"s servants nineteen men besides Asahel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 31, 'But the servants of David had killed of Benjamin three hundred sixty of Abner"s men.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 2, 32, 'They took up Asahel and buried him in the tomb of his father, which was at Bethlehem. Joab and his men marched all night, and the day broke upon them at Hebron.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

"Should Abner die as a fool dies?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 3, 34, 'Your hands were not bound,  
    your feet were not fettered;  
as one falls before the wicked  
    you have fallen."
And all the people wept over him again.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 3, 35, 'Then all the people came to persuade David to eat something while it was still day; but David swore, saying, "So may God do to me, and more, if I taste bread or anything else before the sun goes down!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 3, 36, 'All the people took notice of it, and it pleased them; just as everything the king did pleased all the people.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 3, 37, 'So all the people and all Israel understood that day that the king had no part in the killing of Abner son of Ner.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 3, 38, 'And the king said to his servants, "Do you not know that a prince and a great man has fallen this day in Israel?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 3, 39, 'Today I am powerless, even though anointed king; these men, the sons of Zeruiah, are too violent for me. The LORD pay back the one who does wickedly in accordance with his wickedness!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);








But the thing that David had done displeased the LORD,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Nathan Condemns David');

The LORD struck the child that Uriah"s wife bore to David, and it became very ill.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Bathsheba"s Child Dies'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 16, 'David therefore pleaded with God for the child; David fasted, and went in and lay all night on the ground.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 17, 'The elders of his house stood beside him, urging him to rise from the ground; but he would not, nor did he eat food with them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 18, 'On the seventh day the child died. And the servants of David were afraid to tell him that the child was dead; for they said, "While the child was still alive, we spoke to him, and he did not listen to us; how then can we tell him the child is dead? He may do himself some harm."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 19, 'But when David saw that his servants were whispering together, he perceived that the child was dead; and David said to his servants, "Is the child dead?" They said, "He is dead."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 20, 'Then David rose from the ground, washed, anointed himself, and changed his clothes. He went into the house of the LORD, and worshiped; he then went to his own house; and when he asked, they set food before him and he ate.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 21, 'Then his servants said to him, "What is this thing that you have done? You fasted and wept for the child while it was alive; but when the child died, you rose and ate food."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 22, 'He said, "While the child was still alive, I fasted and wept; for I said, "Who knows? The LORD may be gracious to me, and the child may live."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 23, 'But now he is dead; why should I fast? Can I bring him back again? I shall go to him, but he will not return to me."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 24, 'Then David consoled his wife Bathsheba, and went to her, and lay with her; and she bore a son, and he named him Solomon. The LORD loved him,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'Solomon Is Born'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 25, 'and sent a message by the prophet Nathan; so he named him Jedidiah, because of the LORD.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 26, 'Now Joab fought against Rabbah of the Ammonites, and took the royal city.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Ammonites Crushed'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 27, 'Joab sent messengers to David, and said, "I have fought against Rabbah; moreover, I have taken the water city.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 28, 'Now, then, gather the rest of the people together, and encamp against the city, and take it; or I myself will take the city, and it will be called by my name."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 29, 'So David gathered all the people together and went to Rabbah, and fought against it and took it.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 30, 'He took the crown of Milcom from his head; the weight of it was a talent of gold, and in it was a precious stone; and it was placed on David"s head. He also brought forth the spoil of the city, a very great amount.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 12, 31, 'He brought out the people who were in it, and set them to work with saws and iron picks and iron axes, or sent them to the brickworks. Thus he did to all the cities of the Ammonites. Then David and all the people returned to Jerusalem.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);







Meanwhile, all the Israelites had fled to their homes.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'David Recalled to Jerusalem'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 9, 'All the people were disputing throughout all the tribes of Israel, saying, "The king delivered us from the hand of our enemies, and saved us from the hand of the Philistines; and now he has fled out of the land because of Absalom.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 10, 'But Absalom, whom we anointed over us, is dead in battle. Now therefore why do you say nothing about bringing the king back?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 11, 'King David sent this message to the priests Zadok and Abiathar, "Say to the elders of Judah, "Why should you be the last to bring the king back to his house? The talk of all Israel has come to the king.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 12, 'You are my kin, you are my bone and my flesh; why then should you be the last to bring back the king?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 13, 'And say to Amasa, "Are you not my bone and my flesh? So may God do to me, and more, if you are not the commander of my army from now on, in place of Joab.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 14, 'Amasa swayed the hearts of all the people of Judah as one, and they sent word to the king, "Return, both you and all your servants."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 15, 'So the king came back to the Jordan; and Judah came to Gilgal to meet the king and to bring him over the Jordan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 16, 'Shimei son of Gera, the Benjaminite, from Bahurim, hurried to come down with the people of Judah to meet King David;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 17, 'with him were a thousand people from Benjamin. And Ziba, the servant of the house of Saul, with his fifteen sons and his twenty servants, rushed down to the Jordan ahead of the king,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 18, 'while the crossing was taking place, to bring over the king"s household, and to do his pleasure.
Shimei son of Gera fell down before the king, as he was about to cross the Jordan,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'David"s Mercy to Shimei'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 19, 'and said to the king, "May my lord not hold me guilty or remember how your servant did wrong on the day my lord the king left Jerusalem; may the king not bear it in mind.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 20, 'For your servant knows that I have sinned; therefore, see, I have come this day, the first of all the house of Joseph to come down to meet my lord the king."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 21, 'Abishai son of Zeruiah answered, "Shall not Shimei be put to death for this, because he cursed the LORD"s anointed?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 22, 'But David said, "What have I to do with you, you sons of Zeruiah, that you should today become an adversary to me? Shall anyone be put to death in Israel this day? For do I not know that I am this day king over Israel?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 23, 'The king said to Shimei, "You shall not die." And the king gave him his oath.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 24, 'Mephibosheth grandson of Saul came down to meet the king; he had not taken care of his feet, or trimmed his beard, or washed his clothes, from the day the king left until the day he came back in safety.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'David and Mephibosheth Meet'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 25, 'When he came from Jerusalem to meet the king, the king said to him, "Why did you not go with me, Mephibosheth?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 26, 'He answered, "My lord, O king, my servant deceived me; for your servant said to him, "Saddle a donkey for me, so that I may ride on it and go with the king." For your servant is lame.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 27, 'He has slandered your servant to my lord the king. But my lord the king is like the angel of God; do therefore what seems good to you.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 28, 'For all my father"s house were doomed to death before my lord the king; but you set your servant among those who eat at your table. What further right have I, then, to appeal to the king?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 29, 'The king said to him, "Why speak any more of your affairs? I have decided: you and Ziba shall divide the land."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 30, 'Mephibosheth said to the king, "Let him take it all, since my lord the king has arrived home safely."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 31, 'Now Barzillai the Gileadite had come down from Rogelim; he went on with the king to the Jordan, to escort him over the Jordan.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'David"s Kindness to Barzillai'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 32, 'Barzillai was a very aged man, eighty years old. He had provided the king with food while he stayed at Mahanaim, for he was a very wealthy man.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 33, 'The king said to Barzillai, "Come over with me, and I will provide for you in Jerusalem at my side."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 34, 'But Barzillai said to the king, "How many years have I still to live, that I should go up with the king to Jerusalem?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 35, 'Today I am eighty years old; can I discern what is pleasant and what is not? Can your servant taste what he eats or what he drinks? Can I still listen to the voice of singing men and singing women? Why then should your servant be an added burden to my lord the king?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 36, 'Your servant will go a little way over the Jordan with the king. Why should the king recompense me with such a reward?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 37, 'Please let your servant return, so that I may die in my own town, near the graves of my father and my mother. But here is your servant Chimham; let him go over with my lord the king; and do for him whatever seems good to you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 38, 'The king answered, "Chimham shall go over with me, and I will do for him whatever seems good to you; and all that you desire of me I will do for you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 39, 'Then all the people crossed over the Jordan, and the king crossed over; the king kissed Barzillai and blessed him, and he returned to his own home.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 40, 'The king went on to Gilgal, and Chimham went on with him; all the people of Judah, and also half the people of Israel, brought the king on his way.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 41, 'Then all the people of Israel came to the king, and said to him, "Why have our kindred the people of Judah stolen you away, and brought the king and his household over the Jordan, and all David"s men with him?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 42, 'All the people of Judah answered the people of Israel, "Because the king is near of kin to us. Why then are you angry over this matter? Have we eaten at all at the king"s expense? Or has he given us any gift?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 19, 43, 'But the people of Israel answered the people of Judah, "We have ten shares in the king, and in David also we have more than you. Why then did you despise us? Were we not the first to speak of bringing back our king?" But the words of the people of Judah were fiercer than the words of the people of Israel.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

"We have no portion in David,  
no share in the son of Jesse!  
Everyone to your tents, O Israel!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Rebellion of Sheba'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 2, 'So all the people of Israel withdrew from David and followed Sheba son of Bichri; but the people of Judah followed their king steadfastly from the Jordan to Jerusalem.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 3, 'David came to his house at Jerusalem; and the king took the ten concubines whom he had left to look after the house, and put them in a house under guard, and provided for them, but did not go in to them. So they were shut up until the day of their death, living as if in widowhood.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 4, 'Then the king said to Amasa, "Call the men of Judah together to me within three days, and be here yourself."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 5, 'So Amasa went to summon Judah; but he delayed beyond the set time that had been appointed him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 6, 'David said to Abishai, "Now Sheba son of Bichri will do us more harm than Absalom; take your lord"s servants and pursue him, or he will find fortified cities for himself, and escape from us."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 7, 'Joab"s men went out after him, along with the Cherethites, the Pelethites, and all the warriors; they went out from Jerusalem to pursue Sheba son of Bichri.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 8, 'When they were at the large stone that is in Gibeon, Amasa came to meet them. Now Joab was wearing a soldier"s garment and over it was a belt with a sword in its sheath fastened at his waist; as he went forward it fell out.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 9, 'Joab said to Amasa, "Is it well with you, my brother?" And Joab took Amasa by the beard with his right hand to kiss him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 10, 'But Amasa did not notice the sword in Joab"s hand; Joab struck him in the belly so that his entrails poured out on the ground, and he died. He did not strike a second blow.
Then Joab and his brother Abishai pursued Sheba son of Bichri.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 11, 'And one of Joab"s men took his stand by Amasa, and said, "Whoever favors Joab, and whoever is for David, let him follow Joab."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 12, 'Amasa lay wallowing in his blood on the highway, and the man saw that all the people were stopping. Since he saw that all who came by him were stopping, he carried Amasa from the highway into a field, and threw a garment over him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 13, 'Once he was removed from the highway, all the people went on after Joab to pursue Sheba son of Bichri.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 14, 'Sheba passed through all the tribes of Israel to Abel of Beth-maacah; and all the Bichrites assembled, and followed him inside.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 15, 'Joab"s forces came and besieged him in Abel of Beth-maacah; they threw up a siege ramp against the city, and it stood against the rampart. Joab"s forces were battering the wall to break it down.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 16, 'Then a wise woman called from the city, "Listen! Listen! Tell Joab, "Come here, I want to speak to you.""', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 17, 'He came near her; and the woman said, "Are you Joab?" He answered, "I am." Then she said to him, "Listen to the words of your servant." He answered, "I am listening."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 18, 'Then she said, "They used to say in the old days, "Let them inquire at Abel"; and so they would settle a matter.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 19, 'I am one of those who are peaceable and faithful in Israel; you seek to destroy a city that is a mother in Israel; why will you swallow up the heritage of the LORD?"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 20, 'Joab answered, "Far be it from me, far be it, that I should swallow up or destroy!', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 21, 'That is not the case! But a man of the hill country of Ephraim, called Sheba son of Bichri, has lifted up his hand against King David; give him up alone, and I will withdraw from the city." The woman said to Joab, "His head shall be thrown over the wall to you."', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 22, 'Then the woman went to all the people with her wise plan. And they cut off the head of Sheba son of Bichri, and threw it out to Joab. So he blew the trumpet, and they dispersed from the city, and all went to their homes, while Joab returned to Jerusalem to the king.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 23, 'Now Joab was in command of all the army of Israel; Benaiah son of Jehoiada was in command of the Cherethites and the Pelethites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 24, 'Adoram was in charge of the forced labor; Jehoshaphat son of Ahilud was the recorder;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 25, 'Sheva was secretary; Zadok and Abiathar were priests;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 20, 26, 'and Ira the Jairite was also David"s priest.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


The LORD is my rock, my fortress, and my deliverer,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 3, 'my God, my rock, in whom I take refuge,  
my shield and the horn of my salvation,  
    my stronghold and my refuge,  
    my savior; you save me from violence.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 4, 'I call upon the LORD, who is worthy to be praised,  
    and I am saved from my enemies.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 5, 'For the waves of death encompassed me,  
    the torrents of perdition assailed me;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 6, 'the cords of Sheol entangled me,  
    the snares of death confronted me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 7, 'In my distress I called upon the LORD;  
    to my God I called.  
From his temple he heard my voice,  
    and my cry came to his ears.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 8, 'Then the earth reeled and rocked;  
    the foundations of the heavens trembled  
    and quaked, because he was angry.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 9, 'Smoke went up from his nostrils,  
    and devouring fire from his mouth;  
    glowing coals flamed forth from him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 10, 'He bowed the heavens, and came down;  
    thick darkness was under his feet.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 11, 'He rode on a cherub, and flew;  
    he was seen upon the wings of the wind.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 12, 'He made darkness around him a canopy,  
    thick clouds, a gathering of water.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 13, 'Out of the brightness before him  
    coals of fire flamed forth.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 14, 'The LORD thundered from heaven;  
    the Most High uttered his voice.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 15, 'He sent out arrows, and scattered them  
    --lightning, and routed them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 16, 'Then the channels of the sea were seen,  
    the foundations of the world were laid bare  
at the rebuke of the LORD,  
    at the blast of the breath of his nostrils.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 17, 'He reached from on high, he took me,  
    he drew me out of mighty waters.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 18, 'He delivered me from my strong enemy,  
    from those who hated me;  
    for they were too mighty for me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 19, 'They came upon me in the day of my calamity,  
    but the LORD was my stay.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 20, 'He brought me out into a broad place;  
    he delivered me, because he delighted in me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 21, 'The LORD rewarded me according to my righteousness;  
    according to the cleanness of my hands he recompensed me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 22, 'For I have kept the ways of the LORD,  
    and have not wickedly departed from my God.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 23, 'For all his ordinances were before me,  
    and from his statutes I did not turn aside.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 24, 'I was blameless before him,  
    and I kept myself from guilt.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 25, 'Therefore the LORD has recompensed me according to my righteousness,  
    according to my cleanness in his sight.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 26, 'With the loyal you show yourself loyal;  
    with the blameless you show yourself blameless;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 27, 'with the pure you show yourself pure,  
    and with the crooked you show yourself perverse.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 28, 'You deliver a humble people,  
    but your eyes are upon the haughty to bring them down.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 29, 'Indeed, you are my lamp, O LORD,  
    the LORD lightens my darkness.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 30, 'By you I can crush a troop,  
    and by my God I can leap over a wall.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 31, 'This God--his way is perfect;  
    the promise of the LORD proves true;  
    he is a shield for all who take refuge in him.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 32, 'For who is God, but the LORD?  
    And who is a rock, except our God?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 33, 'The God who has girded me with strength  
    has opened wide my path.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 34, 'He made my feet like the feet of deer,  
    and set me secure on the heights.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 35, 'He trains my hands for war,  
    so that my arms can bend a bow of bronze.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 36, 'You have given me the shield of your salvation,  
    and your help has made me great.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 37, 'You have made me stride freely,  
    and my feet do not slip;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 38, 'I pursued my enemies and destroyed them,  
    and did not turn back until they were consumed.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 39, 'I consumed them; I struck them down, so that they did not rise;  
    they fell under my feet.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 40, 'For you girded me with strength for the battle;  
    you made my assailants sink under me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 41, 'You made my enemies turn their backs to me,  
    those who hated me, and I destroyed them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 42, 'They looked, but there was no one to save them;  
    they cried to the LORD, but he did not answer them.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 43, 'I beat them fine like the dust of the earth,  
    I crushed them and stamped them down like the mire of the streets.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 44, 'You delivered me from strife with the peoples;  
    you kept me as the head of the nations;  
    people whom I had not known served me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 45, 'Foreigners came cringing to me;  
    as soon as they heard of me, they obeyed me.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 46, 'Foreigners lost heart,  
    and came trembling out of their strongholds.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 47, 'The LORD lives! Blessed be my rock,  
    and exalted be my God, the rock of my salvation,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 48, 'the God who gave me vengeance  
    and brought down peoples under me,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 49, 'who brought me out from my enemies;  
    you exalted me above my adversaries,  
    you delivered me from the violent.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 50, 'For this I will extol you, O LORD, among the nations,  
    and sing praises to your name.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 22, 51, 'He is a tower of salvation for his king,  
    and shows steadfast love to his anointed,  
    to David and his descendants forever.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);

The oracle of David, son of Jesse,  
    the oracle of the man whom God exalted,  
the anointed of the God of Jacob,  
    the favorite of the Strong One of Israel:', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'The Last Words of David'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 2, 'The spirit of the LORD speaks through me,  
    his word is upon my tongue.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 3, 'The God of Israel has spoken,  
    the Rock of Israel has said to me:  
One who rules over people justly,  
    ruling in the fear of God,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 4, 'is like the light of morning,  
    like the sun rising on a cloudless morning,  
    gleaming from the rain on the grassy land.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 5, 'Is not my house like this with God?  
    For he has made with me an everlasting covenant,  
    ordered in all things and secure.  
Will he not cause to prosper  
    all my help and my desire?', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 6, 'But the godless are all like thorns that are thrown away;  
    for they cannot be picked up with the hand;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 7, 'to touch them one uses an iron bar  
    or the shaft of a spear.  
    And they are entirely consumed in fire on the spot.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 8, 'These are the names of the warriors whom David had: Josheb-basshebeth a Tahchemonite; he was chief of the Three; he wielded his spear against eight hundred whom he killed at one time.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', 'David"s Mighty Men'),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 9, 'Next to him among the three warriors was Eleazar son of Dodo son of Ahohi. He was with David when they defied the Philistines who were gathered there for battle. The Israelites withdrew,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 10, 'but he stood his ground. He struck down the Philistines until his arm grew weary, though his hand clung to the sword. The LORD brought about a great victory that day. Then the people came back to him--but only to strip the dead.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 11, 'Next to him was Shammah son of Agee, the Hararite. The Philistines gathered together at Lehi, where there was a plot of ground full of lentils; and the army fled from the Philistines.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 12, 'But he took his stand in the middle of the plot, defended it, and killed the Philistines; and the LORD brought about a great victory.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 13, 'Towards the beginning of harvest three of the thirty chiefs went down to join David at the cave of Adullam, while a band of Philistines was encamped in the valley of Rephaim.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 14, 'David was then in the stronghold; and the garrison of the Philistines was then at Bethlehem.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 15, 'David said longingly, "O that someone would give me water to drink from the well of Bethlehem that is by the gate!"', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 16, 'Then the three warriors broke through the camp of the Philistines, drew water from the well of Bethlehem that was by the gate, and brought it to David. But he would not drink of it; he poured it out to the LORD,', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 17, 'for he said, "The LORD forbid that I should do this. Can I drink the blood of the men who went at the risk of their lives?" Therefore he would not drink it. The three warriors did these things.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 18, 'Now Abishai son of Zeruiah, the brother of Joab, was chief of the Thirty. With his spear he fought against three hundred men and killed them, and won a name beside the Three.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 19, 'He was the most renowned of the Thirty, and became their commander; but he did not attain to the Three.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 20, 'Benaiah son of Jehoiada was a valiant warrior from Kabzeel, a doer of great deeds; he struck down two sons of Ariel of Moab. He also went down and killed a lion in a pit on a day when snow had fallen.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 21, 'And he killed an Egyptian, a handsome man. The Egyptian had a spear in his hand; but Benaiah went against him with a staff, snatched the spear out of the Egyptian"s hand, and killed him with his own spear.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 22, 'Such were the things Benaiah son of Jehoiada did, and won a name beside the three warriors.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 23, 'He was renowned among the Thirty, but he did not attain to the Three. And David put him in charge of his bodyguard.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 24, 'Among the Thirty were Asahel brother of Joab; Elhanan son of Dodo of Bethlehem;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 25, 'Shammah of Harod; Elika of Harod;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 26, 'Helez the Paltite; Ira son of Ikkesh of Tekoa;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 27, 'Abiezer of Anathoth; Mebunnai the Hushathite;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 28, 'Zalmon the Ahohite; Maharai of Netophah;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 29, 'Heleb son of Baanah of Netophah; Ittai son of Ribai of Gibeah of the Benjaminites;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 30, 'Benaiah of Pirathon; Hiddai of the torrents of Gaash;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 31, 'Abi-albon the Arbathite; Azmaveth of Bahurim;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 32, 'Eliahba of Shaalbon; the sons of Jashen: Jonathan', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 33, 'son of Shammah the Hararite; Ahiam son of Sharar the Hararite;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 34, 'Eliphelet son of Ahasbai of Maacah; Eliam son of Ahithophel the Gilonite;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 35, 'Hezro of Carmel; Paarai the Arbite;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 36, 'Igal son of Nathan of Zobah; Bani the Gadite;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 37, 'Zelek the Ammonite; Naharai of Beeroth, the armor-bearer of Joab son of Zeruiah;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 38, 'Ira the Ithrite; Gareb the Ithrite;', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL),
(10, '2 Sam', '2 Samuel', 23, 39, 'Uriah the Hittite--thirty-seven in all.', 'en', 'NRSV-CE', NULL);


